.TH REVDEP.CONF 5 "2026-09-07" "emerald" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
revdep.conf \- reverse-dependency scan exclusions
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I @SYSCONFDIR@/revdep.conf
contains paths and library names that \fBrevdep\fR must ignore during its scan. Additional files may be placed in \fB@SYSCONFDIR@/revdep.d/\fR with a \fB.conf\fR suffix.
.SH FORMAT
One exclusion per line. Blank lines and lines beginning with \fB#\fR are ignored.
.TP
.B Directory
An absolute path ending in \fB/\fR. Everything below it is excluded.
.TP
.B File
An absolute path to a binary or library file.
.TP
.B Library
A library name. Files or binaries depending on that library are ignored.
.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
# generated or vendor trees
/opt/vendor/
/usr/local/lib/legacy.so
libexample.so
.EE
.SH FILTERING
The exclusions apply by default. Pass \fBrevdep --no-filter\fR to ignore this file and scan without exclusions.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR revdep (1)
